%%label Movement III
%%note C minor. Interlocking arpeggios in the violins against three even strokes to the bar in the viola. The four-chord cycle is played in bars of six eighths, then seven, then eight; a middle section in E flat gives the first violin long notes; the cycle returns at its longest and shrinks back, ending quietly.
X:1
T:Glass’s Missing Quartet
T:Movement III
C:Lor, in the manner of Philip Glass
M:6/8
L:1/8
Q:3/8=120
%%score [v1 | v2 | va | vc]
V:v1 clef=treble name="Vl. I"
V:v2 clef=treble name="Vl. II"
V:va clef=alto name="Vla."
V:vc clef=bass name="Vc."
K:Cm
V:v1
